WEBVTT

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:14.010
"December 13th - 10:00 AM"

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:25.810
If you hit it with that much force,
you may have broken a bone.

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:27.940
Get it looked at.

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:29.020
All right.

00:00:55.930 --> 00:01:02.390
"Irina: The Vampire Cosmonaut"

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:17.760
"A Maiden's Prayer"

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:20.470
"Albinar Cosmodrome - Staff Dormitory"

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:35.190
We're glad to have you back!

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:39.950
Come, everyone! Let's give
N44 a round of applause!

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:50.290
How was space?

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:51.420
Huh?

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:54.290
Yeah, tell us all about it!

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:58.800
It was hot and awful.
You made me ride a hunk of junk.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:00.220
Huh?

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:07.970
Hunk of junk, huh? Good one.
We can talk about that later.

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:12.520
For now, let's toast with
your favorite oleaster <i>nastoyka</i>.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:15.610
It's not my favorite.

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:20.400
Oh, right. You can't drink
till after your health exam.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.650
That's not--!

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:24.410
Still, a job well done!

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:26.660
Congrats, Irinyan!

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:32.460
Hunk of junk... Hear that, guys?
We've got lots of work ahead of us!

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:37.840
"Albinar Cosmodrome - Banquet Hall"

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:40.470
"Albinar Cosmodrome - Banquet Hall"
Is everyone ready?!

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:42.300
--Yeah!
--Yeah!

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:45.930
The only thing the UK is good for!

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:50.600
--Yeah!
--You like that?!

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:53.940
--Long live Zirnitra!
--Bye-bye, Arnack!

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:56.940
--Long live the Motherland!
--Hear, hear!

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:08.830
How is your leg, Lev?

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:11.620
Well, the painkiller's wearing out.

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:17.000
That's no good. You're returning to Laika
tomorrow, right? See the doctor.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:19.670
Thanks, I will.

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:22.130
--By the way...
--Hmm?

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:26.470
Tomorrow morning, N44 will
go to Sangrad with the chief

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:30.220
to attend a private committee meeting.

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:31.730
Private?

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:35.270
To discuss the details of the flight.

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:45.950
"December 14th - 4:12 PM"

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:48.950
"Space Research City 'LAIKA44'"

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:57.540
Awaiting my return to Laika44
were the usual sights of the city.

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:04.720
There was no celebration for Irina;
just the same repetitive, ordinary days.

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:10.100
The centrifuge I broke was said
to have "broken down due to age."

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:12.270
Vice-Director Sagalevich and Franz,
who caused the incident,

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:16.980
were transferred elsewhere.

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:24.530
Being a mere reserve candidate, I didn't
know what powers were behind their move.

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:30.910
More surprising was that, despite
all the pain, my leg was mostly fine,

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:33.700
and that Natalia kept
working as dorm matron.

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:39.580
There really wasn't
a whole lot to be sad about.

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:45.970
She really flew up there, huh?

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:49.640
"New Orders"

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:51.850
"December 15th - 5:31 PM"

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:56.600
"December 15th - 5:31 PM"
Reserve cosmonaut candidate,
Lev Leps, reporting in.

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:02.770
The Nosferatu Project was successful.
Thanks for your work.

00:06:02.770 --> 00:06:03.900
Of course.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:12.200
For the time being, the Committee wants us
to continue studying N44's biology.

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:15.700
Now, Lev, as for you...

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:16.750
Sir?

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:22.920
Comrade Lev Leps. You're hereby promoted
to candidate for your outstanding duty.

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:27.090
Obey the rules, or you're demoted again.

00:06:27.090 --> 00:06:28.470
Yes, sir!

00:06:28.470 --> 00:06:29.630
Awesome!

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:38.640
The candidate graduation test will
take place on January 26th and 27th.

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:42.310
Only six will be chosen--our Mechta Shest.

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:48.860
Furthermore, the top three will compete
to fly as the world's first cosmonaut.

00:06:48.860 --> 00:06:53.620
If all goes as planned,
the Mechta Project will happen in spring.

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:55.120
Spring...

00:06:55.120 --> 00:07:00.040
With your restoration as candidate,
you'll return to the dorms.

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:00.870
Huh?

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:04.670
The examiner will take charge of her now.

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:07.210
And after her health exam?

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:11.890
Listen, Comrade Leps.

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:16.560
The world's first cosmonaut
must shoulder great responsibility.

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:19.980
Your statements will
no longer be your own.

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:27.730
You're expected to devote your life to our
motherland and set aside your loved ones.

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:30.400
Are you prepared to do so?

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:35.030
Of course. My dreams
are our motherland's dreams.

00:07:35.030 --> 00:07:40.910
Excellent. You did a great job.
I look forward to seeing you again.

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:47.090
You helped me get promoted. Thanks.

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:52.090
It's not like I did it for you.
Anyway, your leg...

00:07:52.090 --> 00:07:56.760
I don't wanna hear you failed
the test 'cuz of me. How is it?

00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:59.720
I'm completely fine. It'll heal.

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:01.850
Fine?

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:03.350
Ouch!

00:08:03.350 --> 00:08:04.480
--Huh?!
--Huh?!

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:08.360
How is that fine?!

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:10.030
It's your fault!

00:08:11.990 --> 00:08:15.780
Cut it out! Hey, that's dangerous!

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:17.580
Hey, enough already!

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:22.290
Oh. It's the experiment.

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:25.670
Oy.

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:29.420
Heard you're back in the running.

00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:32.220
Yeah. No more calling me "reserve."

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:35.300
You could still fail the test, though.

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:37.260
I'll do my best not to.

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:39.850
Did you curse his leg?

00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:44.520
You're just upset
that I went to space first.

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:46.900
You're lower than a dog.

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:48.770
Says the snow bug.

00:08:48.770 --> 00:08:50.230
Who's a snow bug?

00:08:50.230 --> 00:08:52.530
Quiet, you swarming insect!

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:56.530
Huh?! Move it. You're in our way.

00:08:56.530 --> 00:08:58.740
Hold on.

00:08:58.740 --> 00:09:02.370
The launch is over. Let's not do this.

00:09:02.370 --> 00:09:07.920
Lev is right. Thanks to her,
the space program is moving ahead.

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:12.380
We should appreciate her efforts,
just like the space dogs'.

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:28.190
I'll curse you.

00:09:33.780 --> 00:09:34.400
"Irina's Confinement Cell"

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:37.780
"Irina's Confinement Cell"
I've been waiting for you, Lev! Irinyan!

00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:39.070
What's all this?

00:09:39.070 --> 00:09:42.790
Equipment to analyze
her body when sleeping.

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:45.460
When did all this get here?

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:47.790
"Lev's Confinement Cell"

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:51.000
"Lev's Confinement Cell"
This room was emptied out this morning.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:53.670
They sure work fast.

00:09:55.090 --> 00:09:58.550
Hey, what will happen to Irina now?

00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:03.350
Sorry. I haven't heard
anything about that.

00:10:03.350 --> 00:10:05.310
I see.

00:10:05.310 --> 00:10:10.310
Hey, Irina. Did they talk about
anything at the Committee meeting?

00:10:10.310 --> 00:10:11.690
Like what?

00:10:11.690 --> 00:10:14.980
What will happen after your exam?

00:10:14.980 --> 00:10:17.320
--My disposal...
--Huh?

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:19.490
...wasn't brought up.

00:10:19.490 --> 00:10:20.700
Really?

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:26.160
Yeah. Nothing's decided yet.
Also, worry about yourself first.

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:27.330
Huh?

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:31.420
I'll flip out if you lose
to those guys in the test.

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:33.920
I don't wanna lose either.

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:39.760
Could you have sounded any more weak?!
At least lie and say, "You bet I'll win!"

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:44.470
I'm the first one in space
and you were my instructor!

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:50.060
"Biomedical Laboratory"

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:56.440
I can't keep an eye on her anymore.
Think you can step in for me?

00:10:56.440 --> 00:10:57.780
Of course!

00:10:58.780 --> 00:10:59.780
Bye.

00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:13.750
"Previous Day"
The Nosferatu Project
was a complete success.

00:11:13.750 --> 00:11:17.590
"Sangrad - Cabinet Meeting"
The Nosferatu Project
was a complete success.

00:11:17.590 --> 00:11:22.970
Once the original, first manned
spaceflight takes place,

00:11:22.970 --> 00:11:28.680
we should reward N44
for cooperating with our research.

00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:31.600
Following the Nosferatu project's success,

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:39.030
the UZSR turned its focus towards their
next step to space--the Mechta Project.

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:45.530
Furthermore, discovering further
value in N44, Irina Luminesk,

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:51.330
her disposal was again
postponed for the time being.

00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:59.380
However, with the postponement setting
aside any plans for her disposal,

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:05.350
some wished for an "accident"
to protect state secrets.

00:12:11.020 --> 00:12:14.520
"Long Live the Motherland"
My comrades! Soon, it will be 1961!

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:16.520
"December 31st - 7:00 PM"
My comrades! Soon, it will be 1961!

00:12:16.940 --> 00:12:22.780
Let us join as one, uniting to
make this year shine bright,

00:12:22.780 --> 00:12:25.370
and continue moving forward!

00:12:25.370 --> 00:12:29.080
Long live the motherland!
Long live Zirnitra!

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:40.090
What's this about?

00:12:40.090 --> 00:12:44.550
I was bored!
Can't a person sketch for fun?

00:12:44.550 --> 00:12:48.890
It's fine to sketch,
but carrots on a pancake?

00:12:48.890 --> 00:12:52.560
--It's a rocket on the moon.
--Huh? What?!

00:12:53.770 --> 00:12:59.320
So, what are you here for? Another exam?
But it's New Year's Eve.

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:02.650
That's precisely why I came!

00:13:02.650 --> 00:13:03.740
This is...!

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:06.410
Yup! A native dress of Lilitto!

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:08.200
But why bring it?

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:12.540
Isn't it obvious?
To celebrate New Year's together!

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:17.830
Irinyan, you're too cute!

00:13:19.380 --> 00:13:22.630
It looks good! You're super cute!

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:24.220
Y-Yeah?

00:13:24.220 --> 00:13:25.970
Now, let's go!

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:26.890
Huh?

00:13:28.140 --> 00:13:30.930
I was born in Lilitto, too.

00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:37.600
But being a war orphan who was raised in
Sangrad, I don't remember much about it.

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:40.070
How did you end up in Laika?

00:13:40.070 --> 00:13:43.650
I joined the Air Force Medical
Institute after graduation.

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:47.410
That's where I read about vampires.

00:13:47.410 --> 00:13:49.700
I was totally intrigued!

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:51.160
Not scared?

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:56.620
The orphanage teachers were scarier.
They're all like Sagalevich.

00:13:56.620 --> 00:13:57.670
Yuck.

00:13:57.670 --> 00:13:58.710
Right?

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:08.680
Happy New Year!

00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:10.140
Happy New Year!

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:12.720
Hey, you two!

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:15.060
Happy New Year!

00:14:15.060 --> 00:14:17.390
Oh! You're from the store!

00:14:17.390 --> 00:14:18.730
Happy New Year!

00:14:20.110 --> 00:14:21.520
Take one!

00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:28.320
What's this?

00:14:28.320 --> 00:14:31.660
She's Snegurochka, the Snow Maiden.

00:14:31.660 --> 00:14:33.950
Happy New Year, Snegurochka.

00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:34.790
Yup!

00:14:34.790 --> 00:14:38.920
And that over there is Ded Moroz.

00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:43.750
In the UZSR, they go
hand in hand with New Years.

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:45.050
Yeah?

00:14:45.050 --> 00:14:47.130
Bye, you guys!

00:14:47.130 --> 00:14:49.050
Bye!

00:14:49.050 --> 00:14:53.810
I wonder what she'd think
if she knew I was a vampire?

00:14:53.810 --> 00:14:58.310
I think she'd be more shocked
to know you went to space.

00:14:58.310 --> 00:15:04.400
That goes for my hometown, too.
They probably think I'm dead.

00:15:04.400 --> 00:15:08.450
If they had any idea I was
getting along with humans...

00:15:08.450 --> 00:15:11.910
I know! Let's celebrate, Lilitto style!

00:15:11.910 --> 00:15:12.910
Huh?

00:15:14.530 --> 00:15:16.490
"January 1st, 1961 - 1:00 AM"

00:15:16.490 --> 00:15:18.500
"Belka Lake"

00:15:22.210 --> 00:15:24.340
If you throw a pine cone into a river,

00:15:24.340 --> 00:15:29.800
it'll be purified by water
and grant your wish.

00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:36.220
There's no lake in Laika44, so we'll
have to settle for this man-made lake.

00:15:36.220 --> 00:15:39.810
Except it's not gonna
sink through the ice.

00:15:39.810 --> 00:15:41.730
But...!

00:15:41.730 --> 00:15:44.610
--When spring comes, the ice will melt!
--When spring comes, the ice will melt!

00:16:18.770 --> 00:16:20.600
What was your wish?

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:21.690
Huh?

00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:27.270
Mine was to get along
even better with you!

00:16:27.270 --> 00:16:30.360
You really are a strange one.

00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:32.400
You think?

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:33.740
Mine was...

00:16:33.740 --> 00:16:35.780
Yeah?

00:16:35.780 --> 00:16:37.620
Long live the motherland.

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:38.700
Huh?

00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:43.540
You know... "Long live the
motherland! Long live Zirnitra!"

00:16:43.540 --> 00:16:46.290
No fair! You're so lying!

00:16:46.290 --> 00:16:47.460
Am not!

00:16:47.460 --> 00:16:50.170
Hey! Don't you run from me!

00:16:53.300 --> 00:16:54.970
Wait! Wait!

00:17:10.230 --> 00:17:13.110
I hope this year's a good one.

00:17:13.110 --> 00:17:14.490
Yeah.

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:22.040
"The Dream Six"

00:17:24.830 --> 00:17:27.830
"January 26th -
Day of Candidate Graduation Test"

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:31.800
"November 24th - Candidate 2:
Bleeding of unknown causes
after centrifuge training."

00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:33.800
"November 29th - Candidate 14:
Both legs fractured during
parachute training accident."

00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:35.800
"December 8th - Candidate 10:
Hospitalized for hernia surgery."

00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:38.090
The first cosmonaut must be
a hero worthy of history

00:17:38.090 --> 00:17:44.480
who properly represents our motherland!

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:47.230
Strive to do your very best!

00:17:47.270 --> 00:17:49.270
"Written Test"

00:17:51.780 --> 00:17:53.780
"Centrifuge Test"

00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:04.080
"January 27th - Day 2 of Test"

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:06.330
"Candidate 6: Withdrawn for
neck injury during pool high dive."

00:18:06.330 --> 00:18:08.580
"Remaining candidates: 14"

00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:11.040
Hey! Are you even trying?!

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:12.250
Wh-What?

00:18:12.250 --> 00:18:14.630
If not, then run along home!

00:18:14.630 --> 00:18:17.630
--Don't get cocky, woman!
--Got a problem with women?!

00:18:17.630 --> 00:18:23.970
Cut it out. Roza is right. People who
don't give their all shouldn't be here.

00:18:23.970 --> 00:18:27.060
Oh, yeah?! You think you're so special!

00:18:27.640 --> 00:18:30.650
"Final Test -
High Altitude Night Parachuting"

00:18:34.570 --> 00:18:36.030
C'mon, let's go!

00:18:36.030 --> 00:18:37.110
Yeah!

00:18:38.910 --> 00:18:39.990
Here we go!

00:18:42.950 --> 00:18:45.950
"Dormitory"

00:18:46.870 --> 00:18:48.500
I'm sure she's fine.

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:56.920
"Palma Plains"

00:18:57.630 --> 00:19:00.090
How did the planet look?

00:19:00.090 --> 00:19:05.770
Like it was wrapped in
a beautiful, blue veil. So pretty.

00:19:05.770 --> 00:19:09.890
It felt odd to think
I lived way down there.

00:19:09.890 --> 00:19:11.560
I see.

00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:14.610
The stars looked like chervil flowers.

00:19:14.610 --> 00:19:16.400
Chervil?

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:21.360
A lovely little white flower.
You should look it up.

00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:23.240
I will once we're back.

00:19:25.490 --> 00:19:27.790
The moon was pretty, too.

00:19:27.790 --> 00:19:33.130
I wanted to go there,
but thought, "I don't wanna die."

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:38.470
Lev.

00:19:38.470 --> 00:19:39.970
Hmm?

00:19:39.970 --> 00:19:45.470
Um, seeing the moon in space
made me realize something...

00:19:47.890 --> 00:19:49.310
And that's...

00:19:51.520 --> 00:19:55.520
N44! Private Lev Leps!

00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:59.190
N44! Private Lev Leps!

00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:21.720
"January 30th - 6:51 PM"

00:20:21.720 --> 00:20:24.680
"Biomedical Laboratory"

00:20:46.370 --> 00:20:49.370
"Irina's Confinement Cell"

00:20:58.920 --> 00:21:01.720
I told you not to sneak in here!

00:21:06.930 --> 00:21:08.600
What's this?

00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:11.770
A gift for the world's first cosmonaut.

00:21:11.770 --> 00:21:14.310
Th-Thanks.

00:21:17.690 --> 00:21:20.030
What was the point of this?

00:21:20.030 --> 00:21:24.860
There're so many flowers,
it completely messes the smell up.

00:21:26.030 --> 00:21:27.450
Sheesh.

00:21:36.580 --> 00:21:43.510
Ever since my parents died,
nobody's ever held a celebration for me.

00:21:43.510 --> 00:21:49.390
I wish the world's three billion people
could celebrate what you've done.

00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:54.020
More importantly, how did the test go?!

00:21:54.020 --> 00:21:58.230
I did my best.
Now it's just "wait and see."

00:23:47.880 --> 00:23:51.010
"Next Episode:
'The White Rose of Sangrad'"
